# script-src carries no 'unsafe-inline' (the site standard's sec.csp, 2026-11-04). Its root of trust is ONE hash: the
# inline bootstrap every page carries (src/plugins/csp-bootstrap.ts), which creates the app's entry module and
# /consent.js. 'strict-dynamic' trusts what a trusted script creates, which Cloudflare Zaraz needs: consent.js adds the
# loader /cdn-cgi/zaraz/i.js (Google Analytics behind Zaraz's consent box, never under Global Privacy Control or Do Not
# Track), and the loader runs its server's code as inline scripts it creates (as on AXIS Launch and lastmanup.org).
# Browsers that support 'strict-dynamic' ignore 'self' here; older ones use it. Cloudflare's edge-injected Web Analytics
# beacon is not allowed: the estate turns it off on zones that measure through Zaraz (AXIS Launch
# scripts/edge_beacon_off.py, owner 2026-10-30). The inline <script> blocks other than the bootstrap are JSON-LD, which
# a browser never runs. scripts/csp-check.mjs refuses a build with an inline script whose hash is not listed here, an
# inline event handler or a javascript: URL. Violations go to the estate's collector (plus.csp_reports), which logs one
# sanitized line per report: AXIS Launch functions/api/csp-report.ts.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'strict-dynamic' 'sha256-iGzVV5qAmOjWkdFAVwtDv9JcS6Z8T+SMre1UcztURmM='; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://glama.ai; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://api.iliad.trustfabric.ai; frame-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; report-uri https://launch.jonathanarvay.com/api/csp-report
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()

# The build stamp (plus.build_stamp): scripts/ship.sh web writes it per deploy; never served stale.
/version.json
  Cache-Control: no-store
